                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "mixed_conditionals",
                    "title": "Mixed conditionals",
                    "explanation": "Los condicionales mixtos combinan tiempos cuando la causa y la consecuencia están en momentos distintos:\n- Pasado → presente: «If» + past perfect, «would» + verbo: «If I hadn't taken that job, I wouldn't be here now.»\n- Presente (rasgo general) → pasado: «If» + past simple, «would have» + participio: «If I weren't so lazy, I would have passed the first time.»\n\nRecuerda los tipos puros para compararlos: el segundo condicional va de presente a presente y el tercero, de pasado a pasado.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Tipo",
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Pasado → presente",
                          "If + had + participio, would + verbo",
                          "If I hadn't taken that job, I wouldn't be here now."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Presente → pasado",
                          "If + pasado, would have + participio",
                          "If I weren't so lazy, I would have passed the first time."
                        ],
                        [
                          "3.er condicional (pasado → pasado)",
                          "If + had + participio, would have + participio",
                          "If I'd stayed in Madrid, I would have been bored."
                        ],
                        [
                          "2.º condicional (presente → presente)",
                          "If + pasado, would + verbo",
                          "If I had more time, I'd travel more."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "If I hadn't taken that job, I wouldn't be here now.",
                      "If you hadn't passed your exam, you wouldn't be working in Dublin.",
                      "If I weren't so lazy, I would have passed it the first time.",
                      "If you weren't so brave, you would never have left Spain."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "abstract_articles",
                    "title": "Articles with abstract nouns: life or the life?",
                    "explanation": "Con nombres abstractos («life», «love», «happiness», «success», «time», «nature», «education», «history»…) y con nombres en plural o incontables usados en general, el inglés no usa artículo, al contrario que el español:\n- «Life is full of surprises.» (la vida está llena de sorpresas)\n- «Happiness is more important than money.»\n- «History was my favourite subject.»\n\nSe usa «the» cuando el nombre se refiere a algo concreto, normalmente con una frase que lo define detrás («of…», relativo):\n- «The life I have now is very different.»\n- «The history of Bristol is fascinating.»\n- «The happiness on her face said everything.»\n\nComo regla práctica: en general, sin artículo; algo concreto, definido, «the».",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "En general (sin artículo)",
                        "Concreto (the)"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Life is full of surprises.",
                          "The life I have now is perfect."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Love is all you need.",
                          "The love of her life was a musician."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Education should be free.",
                          "The education I got in Valencia was good."
                        ],
                        [
                          "History was my favourite subject.",
                          "The history of Bristol is fascinating."
                        ],
                        [
                          "People are friendly here.",
                          "The people in this street are friendly."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Life is full of surprises, isn't it?",
                      "The life I have now is very different from my life in Madrid.",
                      "Happiness is more important than money.",
                      "The view from this bridge is the best in Bristol."
                    ]
                  }
                },
